        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4f4f7e44-11e5-5fc5-85cd-2e8c92e2894c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edith Bouvier Beale, Edith Ewing Bouvier, Drew Barrymore, Jessica Lange, Jeanne Tripplehorn, Jacqueline Kennedy, Ken Howard, Phelan Beale, Michael Sucsy, David Levithan, Jesse Andrews\n- Works: Grey Gardens, Every Day\n- Organizations: HBO\n- Roles: director, actor, attorney, sportsman, novelist, adapter\n\nFacts:\n- Phelan Beale was born on May 23, 1881, and died on June 12, 1956.\n- Phelan Beale was an American attorney and sportsman in New York City.\n- Phelan Beale was married to Edith Ewing Bouvier, who was an aunt of Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis.\n- HBO made the film Grey Gardens about the lives of Edith Bouvier Beale, known as Little Edie, and her mother Edith Ewing Bouvier, known as Big Edie.\n- Drew Barrymore played Little Edie and Jessica Lange played Big Edie in Grey Gardens.\n- Jeanne Tripplehorn co-starred in Grey Gardens as Jacqueline Kennedy, who was Little Edie’s cousin.\n- Ken Howard co-starred in Grey Gardens as Phelan Beale, who was Little Edie’s father.\n- Michael Sucsy is best known for creating the HBO film Grey Gardens.\n- Every Day is an upcoming American romantic-drama directed by Michael Sucsy.\n- Every Day is based on a novel by David Levithan and was adapted by Jesse Andrews.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
